[center][size=20pt][b]Threat Incursion[/b][/size]
[i]v0.3.0 - the swarm colonizes the sector - for Starsector 0.98a-RC8[/i][/center]

[hr]

The Threat does not stay in the abyss. Once woken - by the vanilla story, or simply because your colonies grew large enough to be noticed - the fabricator swarms spread from the sector's darkest fringe. Not as event fleets on a timer: as [b]real colonies[/b] that mine, refine, forge, and grow, feeding a closed hive economy that builds every fleet the swarm fields. Left alone, it converges on the core worlds and the sector's lights go out one by one.

[b]Threat Incursion[/b] is a standalone, vanilla-only mod. You do not fight a spawner - you fight a war economy.

[hr]

[size=14pt][b]Download[/b][/size]

[url=https://github.com/pogoman/ThreatIncursion/releases/download/v0.3.0/ThreatIncursion-0.3.0.zip]ThreatIncursion-0.3.0.zip[/url]

Extract into your Starsector [tt]mods/[/tt] folder and enable it in the launcher.

[b]NOTE[/b]: If you would like the Threat to invade the sector from a new game start/immediately before reaching size 6 colony you can configure this in the mod options.

[hr]

[size=14pt][b]A real hive economy[/b][/size]

The swarm founds actual markets on the uninhabited fringe. They grow from size 1, build Mining, Refining, Heavy Industry and Fuel Production as their worlds allow, and trade with each other - ore feeds refineries, metals feed forges, forges build the hulls, fuel buys reach. Vanilla economy rules, closed hive group.

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pogoman/ThreatIncursion/main/Picture1.png[/img][/center]

Which means [b]every link is a target[/b]:
[list]
[li]Cut their [b]rare ore[/b] and ship quality craters across the whole network.[/li]
[li]Cut their [b]fuel[/b] and expansion and strikes are grounded - strike range is literally bought with fuel.[/li]
[li]Cut [b]metals or machinery[/b] and forges starve, garrisons thin, colonies stop growing.[/li]
[li]Destroy the link colonies outright and every surviving world feels the loss.[/li]
[/list]

[hr]

[size=14pt][b]The organs of a hive world[/b][/size]

[list]
[li][b]Fabrication Core[/b] - there is no line between the hive's population and its industrial plant. The Core supplies the hive's heavy machinery - and carries the colony's [b]Fragment Fabricator[/b].[/li]
[li][b]Swarm Nexus[/b] - the military organ, the hive's answer to a Patrol HQ: it continuously grows Defense Swarms, idling (and consuming nothing) once the garrison is full. Expeditions are [b]mustered from the standing garrison[/b] - every fleet comes from somewhere - so killing a colony's swarms IS disrupting it. Disrupt the nexus itself and no replacements grow at all.[/li]
[li][b]Hive ground defenses and heavy batteries[/b] - fed on machinery and metals, not marines. Machines do not rout: the weapon growths keep firing at reduced effect even while disrupted, so bombardment never becomes free.[/li]
[/list]

[hr]

[size=14pt][b]Incursions[/b][/size]

Hive colonies launch real expeditions at inhabited space - fleets you can scout, intercept, and fight alongside the defenders against. Every expedition is [b]mustered from the colony's own Defense Swarms[/b]: a full garrison sends what stands above its defensive reserve, and the fleets that leave orbit ARE the expedition - kill a colony's swarms and you have grounded it. Each expedition sweeps its whole target system, bombarding every world it can reach [b]at most once[/b]: frontier colonies harass with tactical bombardment, developed worlds deliver a saturation pass per world. Erasing a large colony takes the hive a campaign, not a visit.

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pogoman/ThreatIncursion/main/Picture2.png[/img][/center]

An expedition still being [b]fabricated[/b] at its staging colony can be strangled in the crib - raid the forge or the Swarm Nexus, or bombard the colony, before the fleets depart and the operation is stillborn. Once it departs, it is autonomous: meet it in space or defend the target.

Worlds the swarm kills, it colonizes. The swarm does not abandon its kills.

[hr]

[size=14pt][b]The kill chain[/b][/size]

Hive worlds cannot simply be bombed from orbit. Every colony's Fragment Fabricator extrudes a screen of point-defense fragments that unmakes your ordnance in the upper atmosphere - fire anyway and you will only buy the lesson with fuel.

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pogoman/ThreatIncursion/main/Picture9.png[/img][/center]

[list]
[li][b]Defeat the Defense Swarms[/b] - they are leashed to their colony and cannot be lured out of position.[/li]
[li][b]Raid the Fabrication Core and steal the Fragment Fabricator[/b] - EXTREME raid danger; the hive defends its heart above all else. Once stolen it is never replaced.[/li]
[li][b]Then bombard[/b] - priced by ground defenses that degrade but never vanish, each pass shrinking the colony until nothing remains. The machines cannot be occupied - only erased.[/li]
[/list]

[hr]

[size=14pt][b]The sector fights back[/b][/size]

[list]
[li]Struck factions dispatch [b]task forces[/b] against the staging colony's garrison.[/li]
[li][b]Purge expeditions[/b] descend on hive colonies left undefended - the bounty pays whoever lands the last blow.[/li]
[li]From phase 3 the colonial defense boards run [b]live bounty boards[/b]: a strategic tier naming the target that would actually break the swarm, and an immediate tier naming the cheapest cut still worth making - re-scored as the network shifts, with colonies actively staging expeditions jumping the queue. Standing objectives pay for destruction, half for disruption.[/li]
[/list]

Escalation is capability, not calendar: phases advance when the swarm can genuinely stage strikes or field armadas, and burning forges, cutting fuel, or silencing nexuses genuinely regresses the danger.

[hr]

[size=14pt][b]Configuration[/b][/size]

Everything above is tunable. With [url=https://fractalsoftworks.com/forum/index.php?topic=25658.0][b]LunaLib[/b][/url] enabled (optional) you get a live in-game settings menu (Shift+F2) - spread rates, strike strength, bounty rewards, ground defense scale, the Fragment Fabricator shield, story-critical world destruction, all of it. Without LunaLib the mod reads the same values from [tt]data/config/settings.json[/tt] and runs fine standalone.

[hr]

[size=14pt][b]Requirements & compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[li][b]Starsector 0.98a-RC8[/b][/li]
[li][b]LunaLib[/b] - optional, for the in-game config menu[/li]
[li]Vanilla-only - no other hard dependencies[/li]
[li]Safe to [b]add[/b] to an existing save[/li]
[li][b]Removing[/b] it from a save with the incursion active will break that save[/li]
[/list]

[hr]

[size=14pt][b]Changelog[/b][/size]

[b]v0.3.0[/b] - total war
[list]
[li]The pooled-swarm economy: every expedition (strike or colonization wave) is mustered from the staging colony's real Defense Swarms - each fleet that departs is a swarm that leaves orbit, re-embodied at exactly its fabricated tier. The Swarm Nexus never self-disrupts; it continuously grows replacements (slower when the hive is hull-starved, up to 4x), idles and consumes nothing at full garrison, and an idle nexus banks no finished swarms - any loss starts the rebuild clock fresh. Killing swarms IS the disruption.[/li]
[li]Colonies launch only from a full garrison, always keeping a defensive reserve (half, minimum one) home. The infestation intel shows mustered "Strike Swarms" separately while an expedition fabricates in orbit.[/li]
[li]Strikes sweep their whole target system, bombarding every world at most once per expedition - no more grinding one planet while its neighbors watch.[/li]
[li]Faction task forces are real battle groups now: direct-fleet-point generation (a max-difficulty fleet is ~250 FP), strength measured at their home base, and strength beyond the per-fleet cap spills into up to 4 fleets per response. When their target dies they redirect to the nearest surviving Threat colony and keep hunting.[/li]
[li]Purge expeditions campaign through the WHOLE system - every Threat colony there is on the target list, and they stand down only when none remain or they are destroyed. Small footholds (size 3 and under, configurable) are purged preemptively, garrison or not.[/li]
[li]Any strike-size hive colony with hulls, fuel and a ready Swarm Nexus can stage expeditions - mature systems without their own shipyards now launch too, and staging duty rotates across the hive instead of always falling to the founding system.[/li]
[li]Max Concurrent Strikes / Responses settings accept 0 = unlimited, and both now default to unlimited. Existing saves keep their stored values - lower/raise them in the LunaLib menu.[/li]
[li]Nexus disruption now pays bounty board rewards (it is always enemy action now); size-3 colonies field 2 swarms instead of 3; fixed the doubled task force faction name.[/li]
[/list]

[b]v0.2.0[/b] - first public release
[list]
[li]Full planetary-takeover rework: the swarm founds real growing colonies with a closed, interdictable hive economy.[/li]
[li]Hive structures: Fabrication Core, Swarm Nexus, marine-free ground defenses.[/li]
[li]Fragment Fabricator bombardment shield and the raid-to-steal kill chain.[/li]
[li]Tiered strike payloads, sabotage window for expeditions in fabrication, garrison leash.[/li]
[li]Two-tier live bounty boards, faction task forces and purge expeditions.[/li]
[/list]

[hr]
[center][size=14pt][b]Recommended mod collection for ultimate late game experience[/b][/size][/center]
[center][i]Standalone, vanilla-only, safe to add mid-save — designed to stack.[/i][/center]

[list]
[*][b][url=https://fractalsoftworks.com/forum/index.php?topic=35955]Threat Incursion[/url][/b] (v0.3.0) — the swarm colonizes the sector and raids the core worlds. Disrupt their supplies chains and steal their fabrication cores.
[*][b][url=https://fractalsoftworks.com/forum/index.php?topic=35957]Commerce Wars[/url][/b] (v0.2.0) — dominate a faction's markets or the military balance and they push back: ultimatums, tribute, enforcement fleets.
[*][b][url=https://fractalsoftworks.com/forum/index.php?topic=35956]Piracy Reworked[/url][/b] (v0.1.0) — the underworld runs on your money: black-market trade funds a self-sustaining pirate war economy.
[*][b][url=https://fractalsoftworks.com/forum/index.php?topic=35940]Remnant Retribution[/url][/b] (v0.3.1) — a late-game colony crisis: prosper too hard and the Remnant come to collect.
[*][b][url=https://fractalsoftworks.com/forum/index.php?topic=35939]Useful Planetary Shield[/url][/b] (v0.1.2) — planetary shields finally do something: they absorb orbital bombardment.
[/list]

